{"name":"Lincolnshire Sausage","hex":"#e3e6da","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sausage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food made of ground meat (or meat substitute) and seasoning, packed in a section of the animal's intestine, or in a similarly cylindrical shaped synthetic casing.","An individual item of this food."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To squeeze (something) tightly into in a rolled or sausage-like form.","To squeeze (something) into something tightly fitting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sausage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lincolnshire sausage","blocks":[{"text":"Lincolnshire sausages are a distinctive variety of pork sausage developed in and associated with the English county of Lincolnshire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Lincolnshire_sausages_and_onions.jpg/330px-Lincolnshire_sausages_and_onions.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lincolnshire_sausage","wikidata":"Q6551285"},{"title":"Lincolnshire","blocks":[{"text":"Lincolnshire is a ceremonial county in the East Midlands and Yorkshire and the Humber regions of England. It is bordered by the East Riding of Yorkshire across the Humber estuary to the north, the North Sea to the east, Norfolk, Cambridgeshire, Northamptonshire, and Rutland to the south, and Leicestershire, Nottinghamshire, and South Yorkshire to the west."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/1388680_Cathedral_Church_of_St_Mary%2C_West_Front_Lincoln_20240519_0252.jpg/330px-1388680_Cathedral_Church_of_St_Mary%2C_West_Front_Lincoln_20240519_0252.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lincolnshire","wikidata":"Q23090"},{"title":"Sausage","blocks":[{"text":"A sausage is a type of meat product usually made from ground meat—often pork, beef, or poultry—along with salt, spi